# Media Query & Responsive Development Rules

## 📱 Responsive Design Patterns

### Device Provider Pattern

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Device detection hook
function DeviceProvider() {
  const isMobile = useMediaQuery({
    query: `(max-width:${BREAKPOINT.TABLET - 0.1}px)`,
  });

  const isTablet = useMediaQuery({
    query: `(min-width:${BREAKPOINT.TABLET}px) and (max-width:${
      BREAKPOINT.DESKTOP - 0.1
    }px)`,
  });

  const isDesktop = useMediaQuery({
    query: `(min-width:${BREAKPOINT.DESKTOP}px)`,
  });

  if (isMobile === true) return "mobile";
  if (isTablet === true) return "tablet";
  if (isDesktop === true) return "desktop";

  return "desktop";
}
```

### MUST FOLLOW Rules

✅ **ALWAYS** use theme.media for responsive styling
✅ **ALWAYS** implement mobile-first design approach
✅ **ALWAYS** use DeviceProvider for conditional rendering
✅ **ALWAYS** test on all breakpoints
✅ **ALWAYS** use rem units for responsive sizing
✅ **ALWAYS** implement proper touch targets for mobile

### NEVER DO Rules

❌ **NEVER** use hardcoded pixel values for breakpoints
❌ **NEVER** forget mobile experience
❌ **NEVER** use fixed widths that break on mobile
❌ **NEVER** forget to test on different screen sizes
❌ **NEVER** use px units for responsive elements

### Responsive Component Pattern

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Responsive component structure
const ResponsiveComponent = styled.div`
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  padding: 2rem;

  ${({ theme }) => theme.media.mobile`
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 1rem;
  `}

  ${({ theme }) => theme.media.tablet`
    padding: 1.5rem;
  `}
  
  ${({ theme }) => theme.media.desktop`
    padding: 2rem;
  `}
`;

// ✅ CORRECT - Conditional rendering
function Component() {
  const device = DeviceProvider();

  return (
    <div>
      {device === "mobile" && <MobileLayout />}
      {device === "tablet" && <TabletLayout />}
      {device === "desktop" && <DesktopLayout />}
    </div>
  );
}
```

